WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Survive in the polar wilderness and reach the relief ship rendezvous.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Search hut stores for food. Carry enough for the next leg.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.000
Take stove fuel. Without heat, the cold becomes a survival risk.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Use the field map to choose the next supply hut.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Travel between huts while managing hunger, fatigue and body temperature.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.000 line:10% size:70%
Ask other explorers about routes and supplies. Their information is personal.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Thin ice can break. Climb out and find warmth after falling in.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Poor visibility and strong wind can force a change of route or a stop.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:48.500
Away from a hut, pitch the carried tent to make shelter.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.700
Use fuel to light the tent stove and recover body temperature.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.700
Rest with heat and supplies, then continue exploring as the days pass.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:08.700 line:15% size:70%
Day 12: the relief ship announces a coastal rendezvous and its pickup window.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.700 line:85% size:70%
The radio adds the rendezvous to your map. Plan the final journey.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:21.800 line:85% size:70%
Day 17: reach the coastal cairn and flag during the pickup window.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.800 line:85% size:70%
Press E at the cairn to signal the relief ship.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.800 line:85% size:70%
Rescued: the expedition ends and the result is saved.

